      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The STAT6 (signal transducers and activators of transcription 6) protein is activated by interleukin (IL)-4 and IL-13, and plays an important role in T-helper cell 2 (Th2) differentiation. STAT6 might therefore be an excellent therapeutic target for various allergic conditions, including asthma and atopic diseases. We synthesized a series of 2-{[2-(4-hydroxyphenyl)ethyl]amino}pyrimidine-5-carboxamide derivatives and evaluated their STAT6 inhibitory activities. Among these compounds, 4-(benzylamino)-2-{[2-(3-chloro-4-hydroxyphenyl)ethyl]amino}pyrimidine-5-carboxamide (2t, AS1517499) showed potent STAT6 inhibition with an IC(50) value of 21 nM, and also inhibited IL-4-induced Th2 differentiation of mouse spleen T cells with an IC(50) value of 2.3 nM and without influencing T-helper cell 1 (Th1) differentiation induced by IL-12."},
